{"kind":"assert","text":"Amendment to S1 (git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b42d3b741986eb8f171e353ad3cb3704f202be9b), from draft 3 of notes/2026-10-18-sequenced-level-and-order-scope.md at f019da60ed08c10fce34123d32f1c2cf1296174f (6.2, decision 18): source order is suppression of an older delivery that arrives after a newer one, not a latest-value guarantee. Done when: a source-ordered handler applies both deliveries in the lower-first run and, in the higher-first run, applies the higher and answers superseded to the lower with a superseded entry; the applied pairs per source are strictly increasing in each run; both runs replay. The earlier wording, superseded to a lower pair in either arrival order, is withdrawn. The late form is as assert b53643f2 states it."}